@* How long a limited box's text is, under the box, once it's near the limit: "550 of 600 characters". A box's maxlength
   (Cap) cuts a longer paste without a word, so at the cap it says the paste was cut; a box that takes more than can be
   saved (a paste box over a saved query, so a long paste is refused rather than cut to fit) says the text is too long
   to save, and that it was cut too when it reached the cap. Quiet until it's worth reading; the status region
   announces only the limit reached or passed, not each keystroke. *@

@{ var length = Value?.Length ?? 0; }
@if (length >= Max * 9 / 10)
{
    var cap = Cap > 0 ? Cap : Max;
    var cut = length == cap;   // the box took all it takes: a longer paste stopped there
    var said = length > Max ? $": too long to save{(cut ? $", and anything past {cap:N0} characters was cut" : "")}. Shorten it to {Max:N0} or fewer."
        : cut ? ": anything longer was cut." : "";
    <div class="form-text @(length > Max ? "text-danger" : null)">
        @length.ToString("N0") of @Max.ToString("N0") characters<span role="status">@said</span>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The box's text.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Value { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The most that's kept.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Max { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The box's maxlength, when it takes more than <see cref="Max"/> (the most a paste box takes).</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Cap { get; set; }
}
